 ## Background
-Coherent Grid Traversal was introduced in 2006 by Wald, Ize, Kensler, Knoll, and Parker in "Ray Tracing Animated Scenes using Coherent Grid Traversal" published in ACM Transactions on Graphics (SIGGRAPH) [S4, S5]. It was developed to address the limitations of packet-based kd-tree traversal for dynamic scenes, where rebuilding the kd-tree is expensive. The algorithm abandons cell-by-cell traversal (3DDDA) in favor of slice-by-slice traversal to maintain coherence within ray packets [S2, S4, S5]. It has been used in systems for interactive visualization of large particle datasets [S8] and volume rendering [S1, S9, unofficial].
+Coherent Grid Traversal was introduced in 2006 by Wald, Ize, Kensler, Knoll, and Parker in "Ray Tracing Animated Scenes using Coherent Grid Traversal" published in ACM Transactions on Graphics (SIGGRAPH) [S4, S5]. It was developed to address the limitations of packet-based kd-tree traversal for dynamic scenes, where rebuilding the kd-tree is expensive [S4, S5]. The algorithm abandons cell-by-cell traversal (3DDDA) in favor of slice-by-slice traversal to maintain coherence within ray packets [S2, S4, S5]. It has been used in systems for interactive visualization of large particle datasets [S8] and volume rendering [S1, S9, unofficial].
 
